# Context for the all-in-one image at ./Dockerfile, whose context is the whole
# repository rather than one app directory.
#
# This file is not housekeeping. The entire context is uploaded to the daemon
# before the build starts, so a missed entry means both node_modules trees are
# copied on every build and the layer cache is invalidated by files the image
# never opens.

**/node_modules

# Built inside the image. A host .next contains absolute paths from the
# developer's machine and would be silently wrong; a host dist is stale by
# definition.
frontend/.next
frontend/out
backend/dist

# Generated inside the image by `prisma generate`. A host-generated client is
# built for the developer's platform.
backend/src/generated

# Tests and their artefacts. Playwright alone is ~400MB installed and exists
# only for the browser suites.
backend/tests
backend/scripts
backend/probe-*.ts
backend/verify-*.ts

# Real secrets. The image reads its configuration from the environment.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Seller uploads live in object storage, or on a volume — never in the image.
backend/uploads

# Nothing here is read by a build.
.git
.github
docs
k8s
*.md
!frontend/README.md

npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
